# figure_digitization — re-fix = panel-local patch only

When the user asks to **re-fix / patch / 修好** a digitization result:

## HARD STOP

1. Change **only** the panel(s) / cell(s) / trace(s) the user named.
2. Prefer a **narrow special-case** (per-panel dict, `if cell in …`, local ROI blank, local `y_top`) over editing shared defaults (`MAX_DY`, global mask thresholds, shared `y_top`, shared extract loop).
3. **Do not** retune global extraction so other already-good panels regress. If a shared helper must change, gate the new behavior behind the named panel keys so other panels keep the old path byte-for-byte.
4. After a re-fix, verify **named panels improved** and **unnamed panels are unchanged** (same peak time / n points / shape vs pre-patch CSV or check PNG). If an unnamed panel moved, revert the global part and redo as a local patch.

## Examples

```text
✅ User: Mi1/Tm3/Mi4 peak flat
   → PEAK_TOP_PATCH = {"Mi1": …, "Tm3": …, "Mi4": …} only

❌ Same bugfix by raising every panel's y_top / loosening black_mask globally
```
